 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5928+) **Naval-heavy-map coastal settling:** On naval-heavy (e.g., Archipelago) maps, settler AI site valuation now optionally add **extra valuation for coastal sites**, as of now especially for the **first city**. This helps early work boat, scouting/contact, trade, first galleys, Moai, or other water-focused buildings; e.g., Cuzco needed a high first-city coastal extra valuation to prefer a coastal Pig + Banana + 2-Sugar river site over a central 4-Sugar river grass site; and kept **moderate for other cities** than the capital after testing showed higher values could, for example, overpull Japan toward tundra coast instead of grass. See [KI#146](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#146---fixedenhanced-base-advciv-issue-of-ai-undervaluing-coastal-settling-on-naval-heavy-maps).
